A||||4||BAM-BAM||85GT third brake light install.....||||1||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||07-10-2000||05:10 PM||||  Well I finaly did it, I installed the third brake light. Not hard at all considering the 85 had the holes just no nuts. I used the inserts fron my license plate instalation kit. It came with four inserts and I only needed two for the plate, so I decided to play with the others, and it worked great. Just have to cut two of the four tabs ( two that oppose each other) then shave a little off of the other two tabs and it snaps right in. Viola' You now have a third brake light in place. All that is left is the wiring. Anyone know exactly  where to tie in at? I don't know if it should be tied into the running lights and brakes or just the brakes. I need a little help on that one.<BR> Any help is greatly appriciated. TIA!!<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||07-10-2000||09:28 PM||||Well seeing as it is a brake light. But the brake lights are actually the same as the turn signals so you need to splice it into the wiring after the brake switch but before the turn signal stuff. If i recall correctly there is a tab on the later brake light switches for this. I dont know about he early ones.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||07-11-2000||08:17 PM||||  Thanks TOM, Where exactly is it that I tie into the brake light harness? I would like to try and make it look factory.<P> Thanks, B-B<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||7
Z||000003||84 Indy||07-11-2000||09:24 PM||||Bam, I did this conv. in my 84 SE it was really simple get a brake light switch form an 86 from a junk yard with the connector change your switch with the new one. Splice in the new connector & run the wires under the drivers side carpet in the factory wiring duct.  the new switch and wire clip fit with no problem wiring for brake lights are the same colors the extras are for the third light.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||07-11-2000||10:56 PM||||  Thanks Indy, I know right where an 86 coupe is. It just happens to be the one I got the light out of. I guess I shouldn't have been in such a hurry. Thanks again.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||1
